{
    "article_summary": "The article describes the development of 'BecaP' (benzhydryl-catecholphosphite), a novel ambiphilic phosphorus radical trap for the synthesis of aliphatic phosphonates. The reagent enables visible-light photoredox-catalyzed phosphonylation of alkyl radicals derived from both nucleophilic precursors (alkyl trifluoroborate salts) via reductive quenching and electrophilic precursors (redox-active NHP esters) via oxidative quenching. The method is applicable to late-stage functionalization of complex molecules, including the conversion of baclofen to phaclofen.",
